["21:00"]={"It was almost \0039:00 P.M.\004 The full moon was blurred by drifting mist, and their blunted shadows led them across an open field, toward dark woods beyond.","Jurassic Park","Michael Crichton"},
["21:01"]={"On the evening before K.’s thirty-first birthday — it was \003about nine o’clock\004, when there is a lull in the streets — two gentlemen came to his apartment.","The Trial","Franz Kafka"},
["21:02"]={"I hurried across the square. Checked my watch. It was \003two minutes past nine\004. He kept me waiting the last time.","Pop Goes the Weasel","James Patterson"},
["21:03"]={"Sebastian remained seated, staring at the phone, willing it to ring. At \003three minutes past nine\004, someone obeyed his command.","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["21:04"]={"At \0039:04 pm\004 trilobites swim onto the scene, followed more or less immediately by the shapely creatures of the Burgess Shale.","A Short History of Nearly Everything","Bill Bryson"},
["21:05"]={"\003Nine-five\004. A voice spoke from the study ceiling: “Mrs. McClellan, which poem would you like this evening?” The house was silent. The voice said at last, “Since you express no preference, I shall select a poem at random.”","There Will Come Soft Rains","Ray Bradbury"},
["21:06"]={"The Parisienne? She coming here!\n“Yes, with her father, by the train which gets in at \003six minutes past nine\004 to-morrow.”","The Ink-Stain","René Bazin"},
["21:07"]={"He just rolled up his window, switched off the engine, and leaned down to unlock the trunk. I checked my watch. It was \003seven minutes past nine\004.","Even","Andrew Grant"},
["21:08"]={"At exactly \003eight minutes past nine\004, the fault, already weakened by the preliminary tremor, now without warning shifted violently and slipped a hundred or so feet, sucking down with it some billions of tons of water.","The Poseidon Adventure","Paul Gallico"},
["21:09"]={"\0039:09\004. Too late to turn around and go back. Too late, too dangerous.","Dreams of Leaving","Rupert Thomson"},
["21:10"]={"She liked to swim most nights just after the nine o’clock news; everyone knew that — at least, everyone who knew her. And the news on Sunday was at \0039:10\004.","Devices and Desires","P.D. James"},
["21:11"]={"These new locks yielded easily to Agar’s attentions. At \0039:11\004 they swung the grating door open and entered the wine cellar proper. They immediately began the search for the key.","The Great Train Robbery","Michael Crichton"},
["21:12"]={"There was a big full moon that night, the sky clear as glass, and at \0039:12 p.m.\004 an old Russian rocket reentered the earth’s atmosphere and exploded into flaring comets with long, burning tails that streaked across the sky.","Beneath Devil’s Bridge","Loreth Anne White"},
["21:15"]={"It was a \003quarter-past nine\004 when I started from home and made my way across the Park, and so through Oxford Street to Baker Street.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["21:16"]={"Leonard checked his watch—\0039:16 P.M.\004 He went to his computer, logged onto his AOL account. Though he’d been instructed not to email, he wrote a message to John. \001You gonna call me?\002 He logged out.","Reprieve","James Han Mattson"},
["21:17"]={"\00321:17\004, Sunday Evening, Angbyplan. A man is observed outside the hair salon. He presses his face and hands against the glass, and appears extremely intoxicated.","Let the Right One In","John Ajvide Lindqvist"},
["21:18"]={"The same thing would hold true if there were someone in her apartment. In that case he would just say that he had been passing by, recognized her charming house, and thought to drop in. It was \003eighteen minutes after nine\004 when Mr. Martin turned into Twelfth Street.","The Catbird Seat","James Thurber"},
["21:19"]={"The first movement of Mendelssohn’s accursed violin concerto was about twelve and a half minutes long. The Jew had started playing it at \003nineteen minutes past nine\004.","Money, Money, Money","Ed McBain"},
["21:20"]={"At \003twenty minutes past nine\004, the Duke of Dunstable, who had dined off a tray in his room, was still there, waiting for his coffee and liqueur.","Uncle Fred in the Springtime","P.G. Wodehouse"},
["21:22"]={"Two days later, on the second of February at \0039:22\004 Jerusalem time, the Dominion launched a simultaneous and massive attack on twenty-two of the worlds between Bannermere and Earth.","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["21:23"]={"My father met me at the station, the dog jumped up to meet me, missed, and nearly fell in front of the \0039:23 pm\004 Birmingham express.","The Secret Diary of Adrian Mole Aged 13 3/4","Sue Townsend"},
["21:24"]={"When do you call time of death on a marriage?\nA hard question for others perhaps, but lucky me, mine’s been timestamped.\n\0039:24 p.m.\004","Bath Haus","P.J. Vernon"},
["21:25"]={"\0039:25 p.m.\004 Aargh. Suddenly main menu is on TV saying “Press 6.” Oh dear. Realize was using telly remote control by mistake. Now news has come on.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["21:26"]={"The terrorists, he began, “crossed the border at \00321:26\004 last night. Four passports were presented to the immigration officer for stamping. Three were of Swedish origin, and one was from Iraq.”","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["21:27"]={"The call came at \003nine-twenty-seven P.M.\004, after dark had swept over most of the sky. There was still a narrow strip of washed-out blue along the western horizon, more like the memory of light, but it would soon be gone.","Purgatory Ridge","William Kent Krueger"},
["21:28"]={"The call had been made at \0039:28\004. This was one more piece of evidence, and an important one. It proved what they had suspected from the first: that the killer was in St. Anselm’s.","Death in Holy Orders","P.D. James"},
["21:29"]={"It was \0039:29\004 and Raphael, entering the sacristy last, found only Father Sebastian taking off his cloak before robing for the service.","Death in Holy Orders","P.D. James"},
["21:30"]={"We have three years of the past to discuss. Let that suffice until \003half-past nine\004, when we start upon the notable adventure of the empty house.","The Empty House","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["21:31"]={"His phone rang at \0039:31\004. Pat grabbed it, and was relieved to hear Mr. Levy’s voice on the other end of the line.","You’ll Never Live to Regret It","Jeffrey Archer"},
["21:32"]={"Geraldine’s bus ride back to the sanitarium, in Bensalem Township, would leave at \0039:32\004. Out of pride, despite the drive taking well over a half hour, she declined to stay until morning.","Sold on a Monday","Kristina McMorris"},
["21:33"]={"It must have been about \003twenty-seven minutes to ten\004 when I reached the summer-house. Ralph was waiting for me.","The Murder of Roger Ackroyd","Agatha Christie"},
["21:34"]={"Thanks; expect me \0039:34 p.m.\004 26th; which produced, three hours later, a reply: “Delighted; please bring a No. 3 Rippingille stove” — a perplexing and ominous direction, which somehow chilled me in spite of its subject matter.","The Riddle of the Sands","Erskine Childers"},
["21:35"]={"The Sergeant jotted it down on a piece of paper. “That checks up with his own story: \0039:35 p.m.\004 Budd leaves; the North dame arrives.”","A Blunt Instrument","Georgette Heyer"},
["21:36"]={"It was \0039:36\004 and the traffic was now flowing smoothly. He walked over to the officer coordinating the shoot for the city’s motion picture and television office.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["21:37"]={"What time last night did this happen?\n“We received the treble nine call at \00321:37 hours\004,” he answered, checking his notes.\n“What made her look in? It’s a terrace, was she passing the window?”","A Deviant Breed","Stephen Coill"},
["21:38"]={"At \003nine thirty-eight\004 the waiter came back and offered us a second helping of cheese, salami and sardines, and Mr Yoshogi who had been converting sterling into yen looked extremely puzzled and said he had no idea that British Honduras had so large an export trade","Pig and Pepper","David Footman"},
["21:39"]={"Fletch looked at his watch. It was \003twenty-one minutes to ten\004. Instinctively he timed the swiftness of the police.","Confess, Fletch","Gregory Mcdonald"},
["21:40"]={"The Whistler’s fourth victim was his youngest, Valerie Mitchell, aged fifteen years, eight months, and four days, and she died because she missed the \0039:40\004 bus from Easthaven to Cobb’s Marsh.","Devices and Desires","P.D. James"},
["21:41"]={"Say that again, Sergeant, asked Warren, although he was pretty sure he had heard her correctly the first time.\n“A Royal Mail postal delivery van drove past a traffic camera at \00321:41 hours\004, about three quarters of a mile south-west of the sports centre.”","No Smoke Without Fire","Paul Gitsham"},
